Here's a simple JavaScript function that accepts text and posts a message via the Slack API to a specified channel:

```javascript
function postMessageToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXX/YYYY/ZZZZ'; // Replace with your webhook URL
  const payload = {
    text: text,
    channel: channel
  };

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  })
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(data => console.log('Message posted successfully:', data))
  .catch(error => console.error('Error posting message:', error));
}

// Example usage
postMessageToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Make sure to replace `XXXX`, `YYYY`, and `ZZZZ` with your actual Slack webhook URL.

