Yes, you can determine whether a Slack message has been read or not using the Slack API. When retrieving a message by its ID, the Slack API provides a `read` property in the message object. The `read` property is set to `true` if the message has been read and `false` if it hasn't.

Here's an example of how you can retrieve a message by its ID using the Slack API and check if it has been read:
```javascript
const axios = require('axios');

async function getMessage(messageId) {
  const response = await axios.get(`https://slack.com/api/channels.history`, {
    params: {
      channel: '#your-channel',
      count: 1,
      message_ts: messageId,
    },
    headers: {
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.SLACK_API_KEY}`,
    },
  });

  return response.data;
}

async function main() {
  const messageId = '1234567890'; // Replace with the actual message ID
  try {
    const message = await getMessage(messageId);
    console.log('Message:', message);
    console.log('Read status:', message.messages[0].read);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error:', error);
  }
}

main();
```
Replace `#your-channel` with the channel where the message was sent, and `1234567890` with the actual message ID you want to retrieve. This code will fetch the message with the given ID and log its read status to the console.

