1. Preprocess the text by removing punctuation, converting all characters to lowercase, and removing any special characters.
2. Split the text into individual words.
3. Iterate through each word and extract the vowels and consonants.
4. Count the frequency of each vowel and consonant combination.
5. Sort the combinations based on their frequency and return the most frequent ones.

