To register your GoDaddy domain with your personal Linux machine, you can follow these steps:

1. Update your DNS settings:
   Log in to your GoDaddy account and navigate to the "Domains" section. Click on the domain you want to update the DNS settings for. Scroll down to the "Name Servers" section and click on the "Change" button. Enter the following NS records:

   - NS1: ns1.your-domain.com (replace "your-domain.com" with your actual domain name)
   - NS2: ns2.your-domain.com (replace "your-domain.com" with your actual domain name)

   Click on the "Save" button to update the DNS settings.

2. Create a DNS server on your Linux machine:
   Install the BIND software on your Linux machine by running the following command:

   ```
   sudo apt-get install bind9
   ```

   After installation, edit the `/etc/bind/named.conf.local` file by running the following command:

   ```
   sudo nano /etc/bind/named.conf.local
   ```

   Add the following content to the file:

   ```
   zone "your-domain.com" {
       type master;
       file "/etc/bind/db.your-domain.com";
   };

   zone "www.your-domain.com" {
       type master;
       file "/etc/bind/db.www.your-domain.com";
   };
   ```

   Replace `your-domain.com` with your actual domain name. Save and exit the file.

3. Create DNS zone files:
   Create two new files in the `/etc/bind` directory: `db.your-domain.com` and `db.www.your-domain.com`. Open each file in a text editor and add the following content:

