To update the `mnpStatus` for each item in the `registrations` array using the `checkMNPStatusAPI`, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a helper function that will update the `mnpStatus` for a specific item in the `registrations` array.

```javascript
const updateMNPStatus = (index, status) => {
  const newRegistrations = [...this.state.registrations];
  newRegistrations[index].mnpStatus = status;
  this.setState({ registrations: newRegistrations });
};
```

2. Modify the `checkMNPStatusAPI` function to use the `updateMNPStatus` helper function instead of directly updating the `mnpStatus` property on the `registrations` array.

```javascript
const checkMNPStatusAPI = (phoneNo, index) => {
  // ... (rest of the function remains the same)

  this.setState({
    registrations: this.state.registrations.map((registration, i) => {
      if (i === index) {
        return { ...registration, mnpStatus: rjson.status };
      }
      return registration;
    }),
  });
};
```

Now, when you call the `checkMNPStatusAPI` function with a phone number and an index, it will update the `mnpStatus` for the corresponding item in the `registrations` array without mutating the original array.

Here's a PowerShell script that recursively checks folders for ACLs referring to SIDs in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain:

```powershell
# Define the function to check ACLs for SIDHistory references
function CheckSIDHistory($folderPath) {
    # Get the ACLs for the folder
    $acl = (Get-Acl -Path $folderPath).Access

    # Iterate through each access control entry (ACE)
    foreach ($ace in $acl) {
        # Check if the ACE refers to a SID in the SIDHistory
        if ($ace.IdentityReference.Value -match '^S-1-5-21-(.*)$') {
            # Extract the SID from the ACE
            $sid = $ace.IdentityReference.Value

            # Check if the SID is present in the SIDHistory of any user or group in the domain
            $domain = (Get-ADDomain).Name
            $sidHistory = (Get-ADUser -Filter "SIDHistory -eq '$sid'" -Properties SIDHistory).SIDHistory

            if ($sidHistory -ne $null) {
                # The SID is present in the SIDHistory of a user or group in the domain
                Write-Host "Warning: The ACL for $folderPath refers to a SID in the SIDHistory of a user or group in the domain: $sid"
            }
        }
    }
}

# Define the root folder to start the search from
$rootFolder = "C:\Your_Root_Folder"

# Recursively check folders for ACLs referring to SIDHistory references
function RecursiveCheck($folderPath) {
    # Check the current folder
    CheckSIDHistory($folderPath)

    # Recursively check subfolders
    Get-ChildItem -Path $folderPath -Directory | ForEach-Object {
        RecursiveCheck($_.FullName)
    }
}

# Start the search
RecursiveCheck($rootFolder)
```

